For example: oc delete pod t24app-5f86f44b64-2b45h -n temenos –grace-period=0 –force

The above OpenShift command deletes the pod t24app-5f86f44b64-2b45h from the temenos namespace.

The –grace-period=0 option skips the standard wait time for graceful termination.

The –force flag ensures the pod is forcefully removed, even if it’s unresponsive.

It’s commonly used to clean up pods that are stuck, hung, or in a failed state.

However, force-deleting pods can have side effects, such as loss of logs or unflushed data, so it should be used with caution.
